    "short_description": "Rate limits by plan tier, rate limit headers, and pagination envelope for the v2 API.",
    "body": "<h1>Rate limits {{ds:component/chip|label=v2|variant=primary}} {{ds:component/chip|label=Stable|variant=success}}</h1>

{{ds:component/stat|value=100|label=requests / minute (Starter)|description=Rate limit for Starter-tier API keys, per workspace.}}
{{ds:component/stat|value=1,000|label=requests / minute (Standard)|description=Default rate limit for Standard-tier API keys, per workspace.}}
{{ds:component/stat|value=10,000+|label=requests / minute (Enterprise)|description=Custom rate limit for Enterprise-tier API keys, per workspace.}}

<h2 id="headers">Rate limit headers</h2>
<p>Every response includes <code>X-RateLimit-Limit</code>, <code>X-RateLimit-Remaining</code>, and <code>X-RateLimit-Reset</code>. A request over the limit returns <code>429 Too Many Requests</code> with a <code>Retry-After</code> header.</p>
<p>To view limits across all plan tiers or what happens when an account exceeds its quota, see the <a href="{{cms:item/5a841201-8328-4b4b-9ab9-035f951c5236}}">Quotas &amp; billing</a> reference.</p>

<h2 id="pagination">Pagination</h2>
<p>List endpoints (<a href="{{cms:item/a47fb2db-0e27-4cd7-b3e9-117cb723c000}}">Pipelines</a>, <a href="{{cms:item/cac7ba67-fc6d-4db4-81ef-efdeef87c39e}}">Connectors</a>, <a href="{{cms:item/55b351c1-f609-4b2a-a238-8ab5e91473d9}}">Events</a>) use cursor-based pagination — a departure from v1's offset-based pagination.</p>

