{
  "item": {
    "id": "a10806ef-f690-4c29-ae3b-378d08146608",
    "content_type": "generic",
    "workflow_state": "public",
    "page_title": "Node.js SDK",
    "short_description": "Install and use @godzilla/sdk to manage pipelines and connectors from Node.js.",
    "body": "<h1>Node.js SDK {{ds:component/chip|label=v2|variant=primary}}</h1>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=warning|title=Upcoming breaking change|body_html=<p>A breaking change is coming in the next major SDK release. Please review your integrations and upcoming release notes before upgrading.</p>}}

<p>A thin, typed wrapper around the <a href="{{cms:item/b9e60c00-c95b-4fe5-8c55-e8affb9bc7c3}}">v2 REST API</a> for Node.js and TypeScript projects.</p>

<h2>Install</h2>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=terminal|language=bash|code=npm install @godzilla/sdk}}

<h2>Create a client</h2>
{{ds:component/code-block|filename=client.ts|language=typescript|code=import &#123; Godzilla &#125; from "@godzilla/sdk";

const godzilla = new Godzilla(&#123; apiKey: process.env.GODZILLA_API_KEY &#125;);}}

<h2>Create a pipeline</h2>
<p>Maps directly onto the <a href="{{cms:item/65a5f692-bb10-4ad1-889a-28a19b3f4610}}">Pipelines endpoint</a> — see the <a href="{{cms:item/c69c120c-89e9-4c48-bac8-ff67efa372b6}}">Building your first pipeline</a> guide for the concepts.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create-pipeline.ts|language=typescript|code=const pipeline = await godzilla.pipelines.create(&#123;
  name: "ingest-orders",
  sourceConnectorId: "conn_pg_orders",
  destinationConnectorId: "conn_snowflake_dw",
&#125;);}}

<h2>Listening for webhooks</h2>
<p>The SDK includes a signature-verification helper for <a href="{{cms:item/6e2fe20d-5b70-4f5b-9216-71f1d0b736b1}}">webhook</a> payloads:</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=verify.ts|language=typescript|code=import &#123; verifyWebhookSignature &#125; from "@godzilla/sdk";

const isValid = verifyWebhookSignature(rawBody, signatureHeader, webhookSecret);}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Retries are built in|body_html=<p>The SDK retries idempotent requests (GET, and POST with an <code>Idempotency-Key</code>) automatically on 429 and 5xx responses using the same backoff the API itself uses.</p>}}",
    "version_token": "500d0d6b-55a5-4e2b-ab0a-e8e3df2cf5f2",
    "created_at": "2026-08-22T01:02:14.685Z",
