    "folder_id": "71acf4c2-42d3-45f0-9086-306921a3678a",
    "file_name": "node-js"
  }
}

{
  "item": {
    "id": "2ba7297b-657c-4988-a7ed-10b9906bdd0f",
    "content_type": "generic",
    "workflow_state": "public",
    "page_title": "Transforming events in flight",
    "short_description": "Reshape, filter, and enrich events as they pass through a pipeline.",
    "body": "<h1>Transforming events in flight</h1>
<p>Transforms are intermediate processing steps applied to <a href="{{cms:item/aaba4e33-be69-4693-8066-1c2f622b674b}}">events</a> as they travel between a source connector and a destination in a <a href="{{cms:item/0881cc13-706b-45dc-b215-08b706dc8fdb}}">pipeline</a>. You can use transforms to reshape payload structures, filter out unwanted records, and enrich events with additional context.</p>

<h2 id="reshaping-events">1. Reshaping events</h2>
<p>Use reshape transforms to rename fields, restructure nested objects, or strip sensitive and unneeded keys before writing to downstream storage.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=reshape-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  \"type\": \"reshape\",
  \"config\": &#123;
    \"rename\": &#123;
      \"customer_email\": \"email\",
      \"amt_cents\": \"amount_cents\"
    &#125;,
    \"drop\": [\"internal_notes\", \"raw_ip\"]
  &#125;
&#125;}}

<h2 id="filtering-events">2. Filtering events</h2>
<p>Filtering lets you conditionally route or drop events based on payload criteria. Non-matching events are discarded immediately, saving destination throughput and storage.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=filter-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  \"type\": \"filter\",
  \"config\": &#123;
    \"condition\": \"payload.status == 'completed' && payload.amount_cents > 0\"
  &#125;
&#125;}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Dropped events|body_html=<p>Filtered-out events do not trigger retries or dead-letter queue entries; they are treated as successfully skipped.</p>}}

<h2 id="enriching-events">3. Enriching events</h2>
<p>Enrichment transforms add metadata, computed values, or static contextual fields to the event payload before delivery.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=enrich-transform.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  \"type\": \"enrich\",
  \"config\": &#123;
    \"add_fields\": &#123;
      \"environment\": \"production\",
      \"processed_by\": \"godzilla-pipeline-v2\"
    &#125;
  &#125;
&#125;}}

<h2 id="configuring-transforms">Configuring transforms in a pipeline</h2>
<p>Transforms are supplied as an ordered array on the pipeline definition. Godzilla executes each transform sequentially for every event.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=pipeline-with-transforms.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  \"name\": \"orders-with-transforms\",
  \"source_connector_id\": \"conn_pg_orders\",
  \"destination_connector_id\": \"conn_snowflake_dw\",
  \"transforms\": [
    &#123;
      \"type\": \"filter\",
      \"config\": &#123; \"condition\": \"payload.amount_cents > 0\" &#125;
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      \"type\": \"reshape\",
      \"config\": &#123; \"drop\": [\"raw_ip\"] &#125;
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      \"type\": \"enrich\",
      \"config\": &#123; \"add_fields\": &#123; \"region\": \"us-east\" &#125; &#125;
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;}}

{{ds:component/alert|variant=warning|title=Order of execution matters|body_html=<p>Because transforms run sequentially, placing filter steps first avoids unnecessary processing on events that will ultimately be dropped.</p>}}

<h2 id="next-steps">Next steps</h2>
<p>Learn how Godzilla deals with transformation and destination write failures in <a href="{{cms:item/5d223f1f-d8d7-4a1c-84a2-0572aa6292ba}}">Error handling &amp; recovery</a>, configure steps via the <a href="{{cms:item/5c640599-6945-4d8e-bd04-c53be4af9147}}">Transforms end

{
  "item": {
    "id": "7524aa93-65a3-4ea6-bb8a-76fdc5f9be79",
    "content_type": "generic",
    "workflow_state": "public",
    "page_title": "Fan-out to multiple destinations",
    "short_description": "Route a single event stream to multiple heterogeneous storage engines, search indexes, and endpoints.",
    "body": "<h1>Fan-out to multiple destinations</h1>
<p>In many architectures, a single incoming stream of <a href="{{cms:item/ef8b84f2-786b-403a-a737-33aafc2e4e2c}}">events</a> needs to reach several downstream systems simultaneously — for example, updating an analytical data warehouse, indexing in Elasticsearch for fast search, and notifying third-party services over webhooks.</p>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=info|title=Independent processing|body_html=<p>Godzilla processes each destination branch independently. A slow or failing destination will not block or degrade delivery to other healthy destinations.</p>}}

<h2>1. Create multiple destination connectors</h2>
<p>First, define destination connectors for each service receiving the stream. See <a href="{{cms:item/93eecc21-ad7e-43ae-a9d5-a0301ad65f1d}}">Connecting a data source</a> for configuration details.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=create-destinations.sh|language=bash|code=# Snowflake destination\ncurl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/connectors \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '&#123;\"name\":\"snowflake-warehouse\",\"type\":\"snowflake\",\"direction\":\"destination\",\"config\":&#123;\"account\":\"...\"&#125;&#125;'\n\n# Elasticsearch destination\ncurl -X POST https://api.godzilladocs.dev/v2/connectors \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $GODZILLA_API_KEY\" \\\n  -d '&#123;\"name\":\"es-search-index\",\"type\":\"elasticsearch\",\"direction\":\"destination\",\"config\":&#123;\"endpoint\":\"https://...\"&#125;&#125;'}}

<h2>2. Define the fan-out pipeline</h2>
<p>Create a pipeline specifying multiple destination connectors. You can optionally apply branch-specific <a href="{{cms:item/08c6f80e-bad6-436b-982c-ba5e22d21ce3}}">transforms</a> to shape the payload for each destination's schema.</p>

{{ds:component/code-block|filename=pipeline-fanout.json|language=json|code=&#123;
  \"name\": \"orders-multidest-fanout\",
  \"source_connector_id\": \"conn_pg_orders\",
  \"destinations\": [
    &#123;
      \"connector_id\": \"conn_snowflake_warehouse\",
      \"transforms\": [
        &#123; \"type\": \"enrich\", \"config\": &#123; \"add_fields\": &#123; \"layer\": \"dw\" &#125; &#125; &#125;
      ]
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      \"connector_id\": \"conn_es_search_index\",
      \"transforms\": [
        &#123; \"type\": \"reshape\", \"config\": &#123; \"drop\": [\"raw_sql\", \"binary_blob\"] &#125; &#125;
      ]
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;}}

<h2>3. Configure retry policies per destination</h2>
<p>Different downstream engines have varying availability characteristics. Set distinct retry thresholds and dead-letter queues per branch to prevent temporary destination outages from polluting upstream buffers.</p>

{{ds:component/alert|variant=warning|title=Dead-letter isolation|body_html=<p>Dead-lettered events are recorded with the destination ID attached, allowing targeted replaying without duplicating events to already successful destinations.</p>}}

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>Learn more about replay workflows in <a href="{{cms:item/c484e924-5ec5-4c95-81ad-c8c31b702a7f}}">Error handling &amp; recovery</a>, or see how to trigger fan-out pipelines on schedules in <a href="{{cms:item/dc9f1302-e173-4034-9581-d06efea7d090}}">Scheduling &amp; triggers</a>.</p>

